{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"45083d81784547d47cd6cd60ccf3dd6ff79e7dd2379911abf3eee6e508a96587","slug":"midlatitude-cyclone-mature","location":"/weather_technology/midlat_cyclone/midlatitude_cyclone_mature.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Mature Stage","content_includes_title":false,"license":{"content":{"id":"CC-BY-4.0","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","note":"All non-code content is licensed under CC-BY-4.0","free":true,"CC":true},"code":{"id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://opensource.org/licenses/Apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","note":"All code content is licensed under Apache-2.0","free":true,"osi":true}},"github":"https://github.com/kgoebber/metpy_thebook","edit_url":null,"numbering":{"title":{"enabled":false,"offset":2},"equation":{"enabled":false},"figure":{"enabled":true,"continue":true}},"keywords":["metpy","python","meteorology","weather"],"copyright":"2026","settings":{"output_stderr":"remove-warn","output_matplotlib_strings":"remove"},"source_url":"https://github.com/kgoebber/metpy_thebook/blob/main/weather_technology/midlat_cyclone/midlatitude_cyclone_mature.md","thumbnail":"https://kgoebber.github.io/metpy_thebook//build/midlat_cyclone_matur-9798f162c82834d07c79178ef6d95a8f.png","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"midlatitude_cyclone_mature.md","url":"https://kgoebber.github.io/metpy_thebook//build/midlatitude_cyclone_-d801d7358c04379444b29422c59708c8.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The natural tendency for cyclones is to intensify (reduced surface mean\nsea-level pressure) due to the interaction between low-level temperature\nadvection and upper-level troughs. As the cyclone matures, the\ntemperature gradient will strengthen, the mean sea-level pressure will\nlower, and wind speeds will in general increase (","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"ROXsxX4EMe"},{"type":"crossReference","kind":"figure","identifier":"mature","label":"mature","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fig. ","key":"eBj3uncIYN"},{"type":"text","value":"27","key":"LrcN0KehjF"}],"template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"27","resolved":true,"html_id":"mature","key":"KhwuGMutTD"},{"type":"text","value":").","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"eNZzfSCw3m"}],"key":"XuqMKHvkDL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"During the mature stage our fronts will have the clearest definition\nthrough a combination of the temperature structure and wind shift being\nco-located (","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"ZTf7rhO2T2"},{"type":"crossReference","kind":"figure","identifier":"mature","label":"mature","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fig. ","key":"u4OAdvwDFB"},{"type":"text","value":"27","key":"UCiJMICfoP"}],"template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"27","resolved":true,"html_id":"mature","key":"cGCXTGHFBi"},{"type":"text","value":"). The cyclone will be moving roughly along the\ndirection of the isotherms to the east of the cyclone center.","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"DG8TU2Gbmy"}],"key":"bFegxJoYU9"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"https://kgoebber.github.io/metpy_thebook//build/midlat_cyclone_matur-9798f162c82834d07c79178ef6d95a8f.png","alt":"Cyclogenesis stage of a Mid-latitude Cyclone","width":"650px","align":"center","key":"I1VQtzzjxX","urlSource":"../../images/midlat_cyclone_mature.png"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"mature","identifier":"mature","html_id":"mature","enumerator":"27","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"WuUCJcC6ba"},{"type":"text","value":"27","key":"pSlo7r9HzK"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"m1t9FUMkdd"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"xSjfSX6rML"},{"type":"text","value":"A schematic representation of the mature stage of a mid-latitude\ncyclone at the surface and 500 hP with location of low-level\nfronts for spatial reference.","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"MSGQif95W9"}],"key":"Cy84ZhRiUF"}],"key":"d2toa45aJk"}],"label":"mature","identifier":"mature","enumerator":"27","html_id":"mature","key":"wHmgO93FuB"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"At 500 hPa, the trough has intensified further (","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"fGHc7d9X3x"},{"type":"crossReference","kind":"figure","identifier":"mature","label":"mature","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fig. ","key":"Ix2JPjelFT"},{"type":"text","value":"27","key":"l5xCmC1Gvj"}],"template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"27","resolved":true,"html_id":"mature","key":"Nk3NJZZvar"},{"type":"text","value":"). This dual\nintensification of the surface and upper-level pattern is called the\n","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"lBijzRcGOn"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"self-development paradigm","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"GJRlSph5ML"}],"key":"Gm8Ak9owbU"},{"type":"text","value":". If the surface (or near-surface) cyclone is\npositioned to the east of the upper-level trough, then the surface\ncyclone will continue to intensify. The overall tilt has decreased\nsomewhat between the cyclogenesis and mature phase of the cyclone’s life\ncycle. However, some continued development would be expected with this\norientation of surface and upper-level patterns.","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"XGdjtvZqfG"}],"key":"GA21BDBKWI"}],"key":"HALHVga7AU"}],"key":"oNCeRYSY9G"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Cyclogenesis Stage","url":"/midlatitude-cyclone-cyclogenesis","group":"Introduction to Weather Technology using MetPy"},"next":{"title":"Occlusion","url":"/midlatitude-cyclone-occlusion","group":"Introduction to Weather Technology using MetPy"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3001"}